Z||000013||88-DOHC||12-09-2001||02:24 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Nashco:<BR><B>Ben...would you mind doing me a favor?  That *shiny* aluminum battery tray, think you could get measurements on that?  Is it homemade or did you buy it?  If you bought it, where at and how much?  Thanks a ton man, in either case!<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Looks homemade, but I could be wrong. West Coast Fiero sells a front battery box relocation kit. Try them, unless you wanting to make one yourself.<A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com/Upgrades/Battbox.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.cwestco.com/Upgrades/Battbox.html</A><P><p>[This message has been edited by 88-DOHC (edited 12-09-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000014||artherd||12-09-2001||02:29 AM||||I made mine, but unless you have a gas MIG or TIG welder, it'll be far cheaper to buy West Coast Fiero's.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com/Upgrades/Battbox.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.cwestco.com/Upgrades/Battbox.html</A> <BR> <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com/Upgrades/Battbox/Battbox_install.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.cwestco.com/Upgrades/Battbox/Battbox_install.html</A> <P>Also, when running your cables, RUN THEM THROUGH 1/2" underground grey conduit!!!  This way they won't ever get nicked, or cut, and weld a 1,000A hot arc right through your fuel tank...<P>Best!<BR>Ben<P><BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Nashco:<BR><B>Ben...would you mind doing me a favor?  That *shiny* aluminum battery tray, think you could get measurements on that?  Is it homemade or did you buy it?  If you bought it, where at and how much?  Thanks a ton man, in either case!<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000015||Nashco||12-09-2001||03:03 AM||||Check check on the TIG; the only way to go with modern metal working IMO.  I also have access to a plasma cutter here in 'bama(not needed for this, but cool)!  I even get free sheet..woohoo!<P>So...would you mind sharing your measurements?  Perhaps a new thread, or just email it to me separately...it would really be appreciated!  I plan on doing that to my car within the next nine months, and that would be a huge time saver if I could get those measurements  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Thanks!<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT<BR>*typo*<p>[This message has been edited by Nashco (edited 12-09-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000016||artherd||12-09-2001||03:16 AM||||TIG rocks, measurments are in the second WCF link  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>I actually did this batt box with a gas torch... just to show off that I could weld flamable metal with fire  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P><BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Nashco:<BR><B>Check check on the TIG; the only way to go with modern metal working IMO.  I also have access to a plasma cutter here in 'bama(not needed for this, but cool)!  I even get free sheet..woohoo!<P>So...would you mind sharing your measurements?  Perhaps a new thread, or just email it to me separately...it would really be appreciated!  I plan on doing that to my car within the next nine months, and that would be a huge time saver if I could get those measurements   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Thanks!<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT<BR>*typo*<P>[This message has been edited by Nashco (edited 12-09-2001).]</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
